# Shell scripts and the systemd unit MUST be LF.
#
# A CRLF shebang makes Linux report "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M: no
# such file or directory", and systemd silently fails to parse a unit with CRLF
# line endings. Authoring happens on Windows, so this is not hypothetical.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Normalise the rest, but let Git decide the working-copy ending.
*.js            text
*.json          text
*.yml           text
*.md            text
.env.example    text eol=lf
